# Derived MVX artifacts — the repo IS an mvx-git account; build.sh rebuilds
# these from the tracked VOC/, BP/, *.DICT/%FILE%, .mvx.
# MATCH THE CONVENTION, NOT ONE NAME.  lmdb's store is a DIRECTORY and was
# named as one; sqlite's is a FILE with -shm and -wal beside it, so once
# sqlite became mvx's default (mvx#187) running mvx anywhere in this tree
# left three untracked files behind -- in a repo that IS an account, where an
# accidentally committed binary store is a real hazard.  mvx's own .gitignore
# uses this same pattern for the same reason.
mvxdata.*

# ACCOUNT STATE, for the same reason and with the same hazard.  This repo IS an
# account, so MVPKG install writes its state here: PACKAGES is the link
# registry mvx reads to find extensions, and mvpkg.installed is a fossil of the
# manifest MVPKG.LOCK replaced (udt/MVPKG.LOCK.H).  Both were COMMITTED, and
# PACKAGES shipped four absolute paths into a macOS temp directory that no
# longer exists -- left by a hand-run of mv-package-registry's test/run.sh, so
# every clone started life believing them (#168).
#
# It is not inert: the committed mvpkg.installed named `demo`, which told MVPKG
# that package was already installed.  mv-package-registry#69's install loop
# restored it between scenarios and its dependency test stopped reinstalling
# demo, while its leaf test went GREEN for the shipped file's sake rather than
# because anything had been recorded.
#
# mvx tolerates PACKAGES being absent -- it reads it with ifstream/getline, so
# no file means no linked packages and no error (compiler/src/main.cpp) -- so
# nothing is shipped in its place.
PACKAGES
mvpkg.installed
CATALOG/
LIB/
LIB.DICT/
BP.O/
BP.O.DICT/
*.dSYM/
*.o
*.dylib
*.so

# Node registry
server/node_modules/

# Generated release tarballs (registry meta.json stays tracked if seeded)
server/registry/**/*.tar.gz
VOC/LIB

# build.sh writes MVPKG.INC/PLATFORM.H before the first compile (the sources
# $INCLUDE it), and MVPKG INIT rewrites the same file in a managed account.
MVPKG.INC/

# The VOC's own dictionary is the platform's, not the account's - every
# account is born with it, and a clone gets its own (mv_git#95).
VOC.DICT/

# Derived verb registration: mkpkg writes these from VERBS (mvx#136).
/VOC/MVPKG
